# ============================================================================
# Secondary Condition Finder — .gitignore
# Organized by concern. Verify changes with:
#   git check-ignore -v <path>          (is this path ignored, and why?)
#   git ls-files -ci --exclude-standard (tracked files that match ignores — must be empty)
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variables
# All private env files are ignored (.env, .env.local, .env.production, ...).
# The committed templates are opt-in via negation — keep them tracked so new
# contributors can `cp .env.example .env.local`.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.template

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Testing & coverage (Vitest + Chrome/ChromeDriver E2E journeys)
# Vitest coverage/output, E2E runner artifacts (screenshots, traces, reports),
# and browser-driver scratch data. Screenshots/traces use the standard runner
# output dirs rather than a blanket *.png so public image assets stay tracked.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/coverage
.vitest/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
test-screenshots/
e2e/artifacts/
e2e-artifacts/
# R-05 real-browser contrast evidence is produced at run time and uploaded as
# a CI artifact; it is never committed.
a11y-evidence/
# Per-run route inventory report (declared surfaces vs recorded evidence). The
# gate writes it into a11y-evidence/; a manual `npm run report:route-inventory`
# writes it at the repository root. Run output either way, never committed.
/route-inventory-report.json
/route-inventory-report.md
*.trace.zip
chromedriver.log
chromedriver-*.log
geckodriver.log
selenium-server.log
chrome-debug.log
.chrome-user-data/
chrome-user-data/
.chrome-profile/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build outputs & deployment
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.next/
/out/
/build
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Generated client runtime assets (postinstall: copy-pdf-worker.mjs) — the
# Tesseract.js WASM core/language data and the PDF.js worker are downloaded,
# never authored. The client corpus is generated from the authored knowledge
# base by scripts/build-client-corpus.mjs (npm run build:client-corpus).
/public/pdf.worker.min.mjs
/public/tesseract/
/public/kb/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# System / OS metadata
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.fseventsd
# Windows
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
# Editor swap/backup files
*.swp
*~

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE / editor configuration
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
.history/
.nova/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security & secrets
# Private keys and public certificates never belong in git — distribution of
# credentials is handled outside the repository.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cert
*.pfx
*.p12

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local databases, caches & event logs
# The embedded event log and any local SQLite derivatives are machine-local.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs & debug output
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
*.log

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project-specific
# Nested self-contained clone of this repo (has its own .git); AI-assistant
# local state; Python prototype leftovers.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Secondary_Condition_Finder/
# Local scratch: isolated copies, browser-driver evidence and throwaway probes
# used to verify a change without disturbing a running dev server. Never a
# source of truth, never shipped.
/tmp/
.aider*
.implement/
CLAUDE.md
.claude.md
.claude/
.opencode/
.freebuff/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/freebuff-sites-build/
/.open-next/
/.wrangler/
# Install artifacts: embedded copy of data/ for runtimes without a filesystem.
/.data-bundle/
